        "original_id": "2db2a62d-3ae2-5beb-a22d-d29a3542ee0b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Iowa, University of Texas at Austin\n- Places: Iowa City, Iowa, Austin, Texas, Texas State Capitol\n- Concepts: founding dates, university organization, areas of study, professional degrees\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Iowa was founded in 1847.\n- The University of Iowa is the oldest university in the state of Iowa.\n- The University of Texas at Austin was founded in 1881 as \"The University of Texas.\"\n- The University of Iowa is a flagship public research university in Iowa City, Iowa, and it is also known as the UI, U of I, UIowa, or simply Iowa.\n- The University of Iowa is organized into eleven colleges that offer more than 200 areas of study and seven professional degrees.\n- The University of Texas at Austin campus is located in Austin, Texas, about 1 mile (1.6 km) from the Texas State Capitol.",
